DMA: chain buffers are reused. A source chain on the GIF, VIF0 or VIF1 channel is gathered into a byte vector that starts empty, grows tag by tag and is freed once the transfer is processed; a city frame of Metropolismania is megabytes, so every frame reallocated and copied the buffer several times over and returned it to the system. The buffers now go back to a small pool (up to eight) after processing and the next chain takes one, keeping its capacity. The bytes and the order of transfers are unchanged. Checked in Metropolismania: all 4 MB of VRAM byte-identical at the eleven views of a scripted city camera run with frame skip off; PS2Recomp's tests give the same results; the memchr and memmove time under std::vector growth (about 3% of the game thread) is gone.

